design\activity\card__3e151ae1-ffa3-42ba-819c-a6973683af03.json:28:          "content": "\u001b[2m2026-07-27T13:09:15.728505Z\u001b[0m \u001b[31mERROR\u001b[0m \u001b[2mcodex_core::tools::router\u001b[0m\u001b[2m:\u001b[0m \u001b[3merror\u001b[0m\u001b[2m=\u001b[0mExit code: 1\nWall time: 12.3 seconds\nOutput:\ndesign\\architecture\\data_saving_and_commits.md:30:Card body, title, header, ordering, and policy edits update loaded files, then `CardOperations.saveFile` schedules them. All files share the batcher: editing two cards before a flush produces one request with both latest versions and a combined message.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_75_position_edit_card_popup_mobile.md:5:title: Position edit card popup mobile\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\B_75_position_edit_card_popup_mobile.md:12:On mobile, the ´edit card´ popup should take up the window size.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\architectural_decisions.md:31:| Components subscribe at the smallest rendering boundary. | Root and layout components compose UI regions and pass structural inputs. Components that render changing application data subscribe through hooks themselves. Do not hoist changing data into ancestors only to pass it downward. | Limits rerenders to affected UI, protects transient state such as open popups, and avoids broad prop chains. |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_data_model.md:18:| Card body editor | [card_body_editor.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/card_view/card_body_editor.tsx:29) | Uses `card.path` as the edited-document target and editor React key. |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_data_model.md:20:| Affects editor | [affects_editor_dialog.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/card_view/affects_editor_dialog.tsx:41) | Uses the card path as the mutation target; affected repository files are themselves identified by paths. |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_data_model.md:21:| Text workspace | [text_view.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/text_view/text_view.tsx:165) | Builds `cardsByPath`, `actionsByPath`, editor-document/path maps, and resolves the active object from `activePath`. |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_data_model.md:26:| Conversations | [action_conversation_picker.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/actions/action_conversation_picker.tsx:36), `ActionPopupContent`, `useActionPopupController` | Conversation records are selected by compound activity reference; card ownership uses stable `cardInternalId`. |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_model_react.md:102:| `header.id` | User-facing card ID such as `F-012` | Domain-visible and potentially editable/imported |\r\ndesign\\architecture\\current_model_react.md:167:Actions execute by `id`, but editing and drafts are keyed by `sourcePath`. Card/file execution is scoped using `context.file`: [action_context.ts](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/data/action_context.ts:17).\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:135:        class ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:136:        class ActionPopupContent\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:155:        class CardBodyEditor\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:161:        class CardPopupToolbarControls\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:381:    AgentChatFab --> ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:410:    ActionEntryPoints --> ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:411:    CardRunButton --> ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:412:    ActionPopup --> ActionPopupContent\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:413:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionAgentForm\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:414:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationChat\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:415:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationPicker\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:416:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionPhraseButtons\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:417:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunHistory\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:418:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunStatus\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:419:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionScheduleForm\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:420:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionSelector\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:421:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionUsageSummary\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:422:    ActionPopupContent --> ResizablePopper\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:429:    ActionPopup --> ActionExecutionService : reads live execution\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:433:    CardView --> AffectsEditorDialog\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:446:    CardBodyPopover --> CardBodyEditor\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:449:    CardBodyEditor --> CardPopupToolbarControls\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:450:    CardBodyEditor --> MarkdownEditor\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:451:    CardBodyEditor --> ToolbarContents\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:452:    ToolbarContents --> CardPopupToolbarControls\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:453:    CardPopupToolbarControls --> MarkdownFormatToolbarControls\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:457:    TextView --> ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:525:    NewCardDialog --> MarkdownEditor\r\ndesign\\architecture\\class_relationships.md:532:    SearchControl --> ActionPopup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:74:- Activating an entry point opens the action popup for the action `id` and selected context.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:5:# Action Popup\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:7:- Activating an action entry point opens the popup for the action `id` and selected context.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:8:- The popup is resizable, with its resize handle placed for the popup position.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:9:- The popup shows the action label, description, execution status, phase-specific log, and previous runs.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\agents.md:29:- Cards, editor surfaces, and run forms use the same persisted conversation and execution event stream.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F-9-actions-popup.md:3:title: actions popup\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F-9-actions-popup.md:14:the actions popup needs to consist out of:\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F-8-signed-windows-electron-package-with-bundled-react-app.md:29:- Update the preload origin/trust check for the packaged renderer. The bundled page receives the privileged bridges; navigations or popups to remote content must not receive them. Preserve `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false` and `sandbox: true`.\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\app layout.md:20:      - body → list of cards or editor with tabs at bottom\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\app layout.md:24:    - number of running agents (with list in popup)?\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\app layout.md:45:      - text is scrollable but text editor toolbar is sticky at top of card\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\card_dif.md:5:Card popup shows diff icon when commits available \r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:3:title: Select workTree from action popup\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:14:User can select the active worktree from the action popup. When the action popup is associated to a card, it reflects the worktree of that card (and also updates it). When the action popup is for the project agent, then the user can select the worktree on which to run the agent project wide.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:18:- The popup header contains the action selector, expand, and close controls in one row; it has no worktree control.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:33:- Test card persistence/error handling, session reset, popup layout and accessibility, project/card execution resolution, missing/invalid assignments, and unchanged primary execution for actions without `needsWorkTree`.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:37:- Card popup shows and updates the card's worktree assignment.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:38:- Card popup disables worktrees reserved by another active card and prepares the selected worktree before saving.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_061_worktree_select_on_action_popup.md:39:- Project-agent popup keeps one worktree assignment for the current opened-project session and does not persist it.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_64_agent_actions.md:23:- The popup sends the action `id`, context, and run-specific agent/model/thinking-level and extra-prompt input to the Electron action runner. It does not send the persisted `prompt` or executable agent command.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_62_action_entry_points_and_popup.md:3:title: action entry points and popup\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_62_action_entry_points_and_popup.md:15:Show context-sensitive action entry points based on `appliesTo` and open a resizable popup bound to an action `id` and context. The popup starts and cancels runs through the Electron runner from [[F-010c]] and links to related actions by id.\r\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_62_action_entry_points_and_popup.md:19:The existing popup receives resolved action objects and calls the React-side `ActionRunner`. Related actions are embedded resolved objects, and the popup has no Electron ex